    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nUI message content is defined as an array of `[attr_id, text_chunk, hl_id]` tuples, so each chunk can only have one highlight group.\n\nA list of highlight groups to be combined in `msg_ruler` would be necessary to support stacked highlights (`%$`) in 'rulerformat', see #37153.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```sh\nnvim --clean +'lua require(\"vim._core.ui2\").enable({})' +'hi User1 guibg=blue | hi User2 guifg=red | set ls=1 ruf=%#User1#%$User2$test'\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIn the above example, the ruler should have blue background, just like in ui1 or with `ls=2`.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nNixOS 26.05\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\ntmux-265color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "The stacking in statusline.c sends attr_id in the chunk `[attr_id, text, hl_id]` but there is no way to see the attr value from the lua side, should we add a new api that allows ui2 to see the attr table like `nvim__get_attr(integer attr_id)` \n\nand then we can just check the table before setting the virttext\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/runtime/lua/vim/_core/ui2/messages.lua b/runtime/lua/vim/_core/ui2/messages.lua\nindex bbc2809467..c5e2790e35 100644\n--- a/runtime/lua/vim/_core/ui2/messages.lua\n+++ b/runtime/lua/vim/_core/ui2/messages.lua\n@@ -587,11 +587,26 @@ function M.msg_showcmd(content)\n   set_virttext('last', 'cmd')\n end\n \n+---Highlight group ids defined for 'ruler' attr_ids, see `attr_hl_id()`.\n+local attr_hls = {} ---@type table<integer, integer>\n+\n --- Place the 'ruler' text in the cmdline window.\n ---\n ---@param content MsgContent\n function M.msg_ruler(content)\n-  M.virt.last[M.virt.idx.ruler] = (ui.cmd.level > 0 or M.cmd_on_key) and {} or content\n+  local chunks = {}\n+  for _, chunk in ipairs(content) do\n+    local attr_id, text, hl_id = chunk[1], chunk[2], chunk[3]\n+    if attr_id > 0 and not attr_hls[attr_id] then\n+      local name = 'Ui2Atrr' .. attr_id\n+      api.nvim_set_hl(0, name, api.nvim__get_attr(attr_id))\n+      attr_hls[attr_id] = api.nvim_get_hl_id_by_name(name)\n+    end\n+\n+    table.insert(chunks, {attr_id, text, attr_hls[attr_id] or hl_id})\n+  end\n+\n+  M.virt.last[M.virt.idx.ruler] = (ui.cmd.level > 0 or M.cmd_on_key) and {} or chunks\n   set_virttext('last', 'cmd')\n end\n ```\n\nThis does produce the expected result",
