        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "This would mean that `attr_id` and `hl_id` are not guaranteed to correspond to each other, and that each client that listens to the `msg_ruler` event has to ignore the provided `hl_id`s and create a new highlight group for each `attr_id`, even for uncombined attributes where `hl_id` actually is correct because the client cannot tell the difference. That's not a good contract.\n\nIf `hl_id` is really necessary on top of `attr_id` for ui2, which I personally don't yet understand, and creating new highlight groups on the fly for the combined attributes is an acceptable solution, why not create those new highlight groups (only where necessary: for the combined attributes) in the C code that emits the event? There would be no need to add new a new lua API, and the clients would not have to be changed and get more complicated.\n\nSince the chunks currently only have IDs and no names, maybe there is even a way of creating anonymous highlight groups in C? This would prevent potential name clashes between user-defined highlight groups and the ones that are created on the fly.",
