            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "After some digging around, #27813 was the point where `hl_id` was introduced to make highlighting easier using extmarks and it became the primary source of info, `attr_id` was derived from `hl_id` using `syn_id2attr`. But, #37153 introduced new info that `attr_id` has but `hl_id` does not.\n\nI now agree that it would be better to fix the discrepancy in the C core by emitting new groups on the fly as the limit(`MAX_HL_ID`) is 20,000 which is quite safe, we can also choose to clean up combined group names when the underlying groups change.\n\nFor anonymous groups, they avoid name clashes, but `sg_name` is assumed non-NULL. `syn_id2name()` is documented to return “”, group listing and completion (where NULL ends the list) would break, and names returned to Lua couldn’t be passed back in to find the same group. Anonymous groups would break the existing rule that every highlight group has a name, which is a contract change. A named group with a name users can’t type (like User1+User2) avoids the clash and keeps that rule, so no caller needs to change.",
